Our learning objectives are:
- Use Microsoft Defender XDR to research file hashes and get threat actor attribution
- Trace malware from file creation through process execution to data exfiltration
- Investigate phishing campaigns and identify targeted employee roles
- Pivot from an EDR alert to uncover a larger compromise across multiple machines
- Recognize reconnaissance activity in inbound network logs
- Identify data staging and exfiltration commands in process logs
- Connect social engineering tactics to technical indicators
- Attribute attacks to known threat actors using threat intelligence

https://kc7cyber.com/challenges/222

Section 1: All Fun & Games
What was the name of the game that James mentioned in his LinkedIn post?
This was given in a screenshot on the previous page: DeTankWar

What is James' hostname?
Employees
| where name == "James Douglas"
Answer: UB9I-DESKTOP
For future reference: IP - 10.10.0.10, email address - james_douglas@titanshield.com, username - jadouglas, role - Lead Defense Engineer, MFA enabled - False

How many results did this query return?
FileCreationEvents
| where hostname == "<JAMES' HOSTNAME HERE>"
